265756750d6f54ff5ebf8622ad3ad582135e809c196ad6c58a4425e1a85784bb
Generated table: 96 entries, 4,250 UTF-8 bytes; one ambiguous ID omitted.
The derivative table uses the 16-bit program-header game ID, not the retail
catalogue number. Normal commercial NGCD numbers use BCD; publisher-specific
catalogue numbers and Fatal Fury 3 require explicit hardware-ID mappings.
These factual mappings were cross-checked against:
https://github.com/finalburnneo/FBNeo/blob/4033bc427be0538d637eceed40c430c4837d0780/src/burner/neocdlist_games.h
No FBNeo code or title table is included or linked. Titles come only from
the pinned Libretro DAT. Region, language and revision labels are removed
because the program ID does not distinguish those retail variants. Different
remaining names for an ID are omitted and recorded in neocd-title-collisions.json.
Unknown homebrew catalogue-to-header mappings are omitted.
Treasure of the Caribbean reuses Janshin's hardware ID 0x0048; both titles
are recorded as an ambiguous ID and omitted from the runtime table.

